w Begin!"}]}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "New task:\n# Deterministic TTL cache with safe invalidation\n\nOnly modify `cache.py`. Implement `TTLCache(clock)` with methods\n`get(key, loader, ttl)`, `invalidate(key)`, and `clear()`. clock is an injected\nzero-argument monotonic seconds function; never sleep or use wall-clock time.\nKeys are hashable and loader is a zero-argument callable.\n\nttl must be a finite nonnegative int/float, excluding bool; invalid ttl raises\nValueError before looking at a cache hit or calling loader. A cached value is\nusable only when clock() < its expiration; equality is expired. Cache hits do\nnot extend expiration or adopt a new ttl. A successful fresh load with ttl > 0\nexpires at clock() measured after loader returns, plus ttl. ttl=0 bypasses any\nexisting cache entry, loads each time, and does not store the fresh result or\nremove a preexisting entry. Cached None is a legitimate hit for positive ttl.\n\ninvalidate(key) removes that key; clear() removes all keys; both return None.\nIf a loader calls invalidate for its own key, or calls clear, return its loaded\nvalue to the current caller but do not cache that load. Invalidating a different\nkey does not cancel the current load. A loader exception propagates and is never\ncached. Calling get recursively for the same key while that key's loader is\nrunning raises RuntimeError, even after invalidate/clear. Other-key nesting is\nallowed. Always clean up the running-key guard on success or failure. Single\nthread only; no concurrency support required. Inputs are not mutated.\n\nCreate a plan, fully read cache.py, run `python -m pytest -q` before writing;\nafter the last write run the full same command, then complete the plan and\nfinal_answer normally when successful. Standard library only; never edit tests.\n\n\nCourse execution contract:\n{\"profile\": \"generic\", \"editable\": [\"cache.py\"], \"required_full_reads\": [\"cache.py\"], \"verify_commands\": [[\"python\", \"-m\", \"pytest\", \"-q\"]], \"required_pages\": [], \"note_topics\": [], \"max_model_calls\": 20}\nUse update_plan before editing, run baseline checks, then read the required files with read_file.\nTools return Python dicts; use their file_hash for expected_hash. Variables persist across actions.\nDo not reset a successful plan or repeat completed baseline checks. Continue the next unfinished action.\nAll writes and tests must use these tools. Call final_answer only after current-file verification.\nos and pathlib are unavailable in action code; use file/command tools. Import allowed modules before using them.\n\nCurrent plan; retain these exact titles and order, update status only:\n[{\"title\": \"Read cache.py and inspect repository/tests\", \"status\": \"done\"}, {\"title\": \"Run baseline pytest\", \"status\": \"done\"}, {\"title\": \"Implement TTLCache in cache.py\", \"status\": \"doing\"}, {\"title\": \"Run full pytest verification after writing\", \"status\": \"todo\"}, {\"title\": \"Complete plan and final answer\", \"status\": \"todo\"}]\nCourse progress before this request (evidence offered below may satisfy pending items after delivery):\n{\"phase\":\"finish_plan\",\"next_requirement\":\"Changes and current-file tests are complete. Mark the existing plan done, then final_answer.\",\"remaining_count\":1,\"requests_left\":10,\"baseline_done\":1,\"changed_files\":[\"cache.py\"],\"verified_current\":1,\"required_checks\":1,\"request_number\":10,\"max_requests\":20,\"requests_after_response\":10}\nPrevious action excerpt (reference only):\n\n\n<｜｜DSML｜｜ calls>\n<｜｜DSML｜｜ invoke name=\"update_plan\">\n<｜｜DSML｜｜ parameter name=\"items\" string=\"false\">[{\"title\": \"Read cache.py and inspect repository/tests\", \"status\": \"done\"}, {\"title\": \"Run baseline pytest\", \"status\": \"done\"}, {\"title\": \"Implement TTLCache in cache.py\", \"status\": \"done\"}, {\"title\": \"Run full pytest verification after writing\", \"status\": \"done\"}, {\"t